#: src/development/glossary.md:3
msgid "Zed Development: Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:5
msgid ""
"This page defines terms and structures used throughout the Zed codebase."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:7
msgid "It is a best-effort list and a work in progress."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:18
msgid "Naming conventions"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:20
msgid ""
"These are common naming patterns across the codebase. `Name` is a "
"placeholder for any type name, such as `AnyElement` or `LspStore`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:23
msgid "`AnyName`: A type-erased version of _name_. Think `Box<dyn NameTrait>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:24
msgid ""
"`NameStore`: A wrapper type which abstracts over whether operations are "
"running locally or on a remote."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:26
msgid "GPUI"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:28
msgid "State management"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:30
msgid ""
"`App`: A singleton that holds full application state, including all "
"entities. `App` is not `Send`, so it exists only on the thread that created "
"it (usually the main/UI thread). If you see `&mut App`, you are on the UI "
"thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:31
msgid ""
"`Context`: A wrapper around `App` with specialized behavior for a specific "
"`Entity`. You can think of it as `(&mut App, Entity<V>)`. For example, `App::"
"spawn` takes `AsyncFnOnce(AsyncApp) -> Ret`, while `Context::spawn` takes "
"`AsyncFnOnce(WeakEntity<V>, AsyncApp) -> Ret`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:32
msgid ""
"`AsyncApp`: An owned version of `App` for async contexts. It is still not "
"`Send`, so it still runs on the main thread, and operations may fail if the "
"`App` has already terminated. `AsyncApp` exists because `App` is usually "
"accessed as `&mut App`, which is awkward to hold across async boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:34
msgid ""
"`AppContext`: A trait that abstracts over `App`, `AsyncApp`, `Context`, and "
"their test variants."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:35
msgid ""
"`Task`: A future running (or scheduled to run) on a background or foreground "
"executor. Unlike regular futures, tasks do not need `.await` to start. You "
"still need to await them to read their result."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:36
msgid ""
"`Executor`: Used to spawn tasks that run either on the foreground or "
"background thread. Try to run the tasks on the background thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:37
msgid "`BackgroundExecutor`: A threadpool running `Task`s."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:38
msgid "`ForegroundExecutor`: The main thread running `Task`s."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:39
msgid ""
"`Entity`: A strong, well-typed reference to a struct which is managed by "
"gpui. Effectively a pointer/map key into the `App::EntityMap`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:40
msgid ""
"`WeakEntity`: A runtime checked reference to an `Entity` which may no longer "
"exist. Similar to [`std::rc::Weak`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/rc/struct."
"Weak.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:41
msgid ""
"`Global`: A singleton type which has only one value, that is stored in the "
"`App`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:42
msgid "`Event`: A data type that can be sent by an `Entity` to subscribers."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:43
msgid ""
"`Action`: An event that represents a user's keyboard input that can be "
"handled by listeners Example: `file finder: toggle`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:45
msgid "`Observing`: Reacting to notifications that entities have changed."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:46
msgid ""
"`Subscription`: An event handler that is used to react to the changes of "
"state in the application."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:47
msgid "Emitted event handling"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:48
msgid "Observing `{new,release,on notify}` of an entity"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:50
msgid "UI"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:52
msgid ""
"`View`: An `Entity` which can produce an `Element` through its "
"implementation of `Render`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:53
msgid "`Element`: A type that can be laid out and painted to the screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:54
msgid ""
"`element expression`: An expression that builds an element tree, example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:68
msgid ""
"`Component`: A builder which can be rendered turning it into an `Element`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:69
msgid "`Dispatch tree`: TODO"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:70
msgid "`Focus`: The place where keystrokes are handled first"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:71
msgid ""
"`Focus tree`: Path from the place that has the current focus to the UI Root. "
"Example <img> TODO"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:73
msgid "Zed UI"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:75
msgid ""
"`Window`: A struct representing a Zed window in your desktop environment "
"(see image below). You can have multiple windows open. This is mostly passed "
"around for rendering."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:76
msgid "`Modal`: A UI element that floats on top of the rest of the UI"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:77
msgid ""
"`Picker`: A struct representing a list of items floating on top of the UI "
"(Modal). You can select an item and confirm. What happens on select or "
"confirm is determined by the picker's delegate. (The 'Modal' in the image "
"below is a picker.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:78
msgid ""
"`PickerDelegate`: A trait used to specialize behavior for a `Picker`. The "
"`Picker` stores the `PickerDelegate` in the field delegate."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:79
msgid ""
"`Center`: The middle of the zed window, the center is split into multiple "
"`Pane`s. In the codebase this is a field on the `Workspace` struct. (see "
"image below)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:80
msgid ""
"`Pane`: An area in the `Center` where we can place items, such as an editor, "
"multi-buffer or terminal (see image below)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:81
msgid ""
"`Panel`: An `Entity` implementing the `Panel` trait. Panels can be placed in "
"a `Dock`. In the image below: `ProjectPanel` is in the left dock, "
"`DebugPanel` is in the bottom dock, and `AgentPanel` is in the right dock. "
"`Editor` does not implement `Panel`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:82
msgid ""
"`Dock`: A UI element similar to a `Pane` that can be opened and hidden. Up "
"to three docks can be open at once: left, right, and bottom. A dock contains "
"one or more `Panel`s, not `Pane`s."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:86
msgid "`Project`: One or more `Worktree`s"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:87
msgid "`Worktree`: Represents either local or remote files."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:91
msgid ""
"[Multibuffer](https://zed.dev/docs/multibuffers): A list of Editors, a multi-"
"buffer allows editing multiple files simultaneously. A multi-buffer opens "
"when an operation in Zed returns multiple locations, examples: _search_ or "
"_go to definition_. See project search in the image below."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:95
msgid "Editor"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:97
msgid ""
"`Editor`: The text editor type. Most editable surfaces in Zed are an "
"`Editor`, including single-line inputs. Each pane in the image above "
"contains one or more `Editor` instances."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:98
msgid "`Workspace`: The root of the window"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:99
msgid "`Entry`: A file, dir, pending dir or unloaded dir."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:100
msgid ""
"`Buffer`: The in-memory representation of a 'file' together with relevant "
"data such as syntax trees, git status and diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:101
msgid ""
"`pending selection`: You have mouse down and you're dragging but you have "
"not yet released."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:103
msgid "Collab"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:105
msgid "`Collab session`: Multiple users working in a shared `Project`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:106
msgid "`Upstream client`: The zed client which has shared their workspace"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:107
msgid "`Downstream client`: The zed client joining a shared workspace"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:109
msgid "Debugger"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:111
msgid "`DapStore`: Is an entity that manages debugger sessions"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:112
msgid ""
"`debugger::Session`: An entity that manages the lifecycle of a debug session "
"and communication with DAPs."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:113
msgid ""
"`BreakpointStore`: Is an entity that manages breakpoints states in local and "
"remote instances of Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:114
msgid "`DebugSession`: Manages a debug session's UI and running state"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:115
msgid "`RunningState`: Directly manages all the views of a debug session"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:116
msgid "`VariableList`: The variable and watch list view of a debug session"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:117
msgid "`Console`: TODO"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:118
msgid "`Terminal`: TODO"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/glossary.md:119
msgid "`BreakpointList`: TODO"
msgstr ""
